    {
      "title": "Notion DNA Inheritance",
      "content": "Super deliberately inherits Notion's exact workspace palette — #f9f9f8 canvas and #37352f text — as a visual handshake with its parent tool. Users who publish from Notion should feel their content's aesthetic continuity preserved. The system extends this inherited palette with a sunlit amber accent and a more typographically confident display voice, signaling that Super is the publication layer, not just a wrapper. When designing new screens, preserve the Notion-paper feel in any context that shows source content or editor interfaces; introduce Super's editorial display type and amber accent only in the published-site framing."
